\f6 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  Error\
\ls39\ilvl0
\f5\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 Blue 
\f6 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  Information\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Never use semantic colors as branding elements.\
\
\pard\pardeftab560\sa40\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32 \cf0 Backgrounds\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs26 \cf0 Prefer clean, light backgrounds with generous whitespace.\
Cards should remain white with subtle borders or soft shadows.\
Avoid colorful backgrounds unless used for onboarding or celebration screens.\
\
\pard\pardeftab560\sa40\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32 \cf0 Charts & Analytics\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs26 \cf0 Use the primary brand color for the primary metric.\
Use semantic colors only when representing meaningful status (e.g., success, warning, or error).\
Avoid rainbow-colored charts.\
\
\pard\pardeftab560\sa40\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32 \cf0 Accessibility\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs26 \cf0 Ensure all text and UI components meet 
\f0\b WCAG AA
\f1\b0  contrast standards.\
Do not rely solely on color to convey meaning. Always pair color with icons, labels, or supporting text.\
\
I would make 
\f0\b one small change
\f1\b0  to the primary color though.\
Instead of 
\f0\b\fs32 #5B5BD6
\f1\b0\fs26 , I'd use 
\f0\b\fs32 #6366F1
\fs26  (Indigo 500)
\f1\b0 .\
Reasons:\
\pard\pardeftab560\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls40\ilvl0
\f5\fs18 \cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 It feels slightly more modern and polished.\
\ls40\ilvl0
\f5\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 It pairs beautifully with both light and dark themes.\
\ls40\ilvl0
\f5\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 It works exceptionally well with shadcn/ui and Tailwind.\
\ls40\ilvl0
\f5\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 It's vibrant enough for progress rings without becoming overwhelming.\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 It's a subtle difference, but for a productivity app inspired by Apple, Linear, and Notion, 
\f0\b\fs32 #6366F1
\f1\b0\fs26  gives a cleaner and more refined visual identity.\
